["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>You cannot hunt what you cannot name in half a second. This chapter makes a white tail obvious at 200 m.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-buck-side.jpg\" alt=\"White tailed deer buck, side view, New Jersey. Brown tail with white edges, antler tines rising from one main beam.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>White tailed deer buck, side view, New Jersey. Brown tail with white edges, antler tines rising from one main beam. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Famartin, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025-11-09_07_48_17_White-tailed_Deer_buck_in_autumn_along_Aquetong_Lane_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township,_Mercer_County,_New_Jersey.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>10 chapters. This is chapter 1: who the white tail is.</li><li>Quick version first? <a href=\"#/s/white-tailed-deer\">White tailed deer</a>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the 10 chapters cover</summary><ol><li>Meet the animal (this one): ID, look alikes, size, BC numbers.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-02\">The body</a>: bones, lungs, heart, rumen, fat.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-03\">The senses</a>: nose, ears, eyes and how to beat each.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-04\">The mind</a>: alarm, pressure, family life, old bucks.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-05\">The year</a>: month by month, antlers, rut, fawns.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-06\">The day</a>: bed, feed, weather, moon, pressure.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-07\">Where they are</a>: habitat, foods, your 3 regions, the Hunt Map.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-08\">Sign and tracking</a>: tracks, beds, rubs, scrapes, following.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-09\">How to hunt them</a>: every method step by step.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-10\">Shot to table and the rules</a>: placement, tracking, meat, rules, cheat sheet.</li></ol><ul><li>Each chapter ends with memory hooks and a 5 question quiz.</li><li>Flashcards: the White tail Masterclass deck.</li><li>Mule deer share most of the body plan. Their Masterclass is chapter by chapter alongside this one, for example <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-02\">Mule deer Masterclass 2</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-buck-front.jpg\" alt=\"Buck: tines rise off one main beam.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Buck: tines rise off one main beam. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Famartin, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2024-11-08_10_54_30_White-tailed_Deer_buck_along_Montague_Avenue_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township,_Mercer_County,_New_Jersey.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-doe.jpg\" alt=\"Doe: no antlers, wide brown tail.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Doe: no antlers, wide brown tail. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service - Midwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White-tailed_deer_(54365597311).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-doe-flag.jpg\" alt=\"Alarm: the white flag goes up.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Alarm: the white flag goes up. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: HARRY W. McCORMACK ( TEABERRYEAGLE ), CC BY 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EASTERN_WHITETAIL_DEER_-_A_DOE_WITH_TAIL_UP,_THE_WHITE_FLAG_OF_ALARM.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-run.jpg\" alt=\"Runs low and smooth, no bounce.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Runs low and smooth, no bounce. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2_White-tailed_deer_run_past_the_Indian_Memorial._(74cf0194-1dd8-b71b-0b1f-3242b5474cf7).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Buck: antlers September to winter <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Doe: no antlers. Fawn: spots fade by fall <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul>","<details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ID by sex and age</summary><ul><li><strong>Buck</strong> (male): hard antlers from about September until they drop, January to March (75%, see chapter 5).</li><li><strong>Doe</strong> (female): no antlers. Longer, slimmer face (Tip).</li><li><strong>Fawn</strong> (under 1 year): born late May or June with white spots (85%, BC account). Spots fade with the first fall coat <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><strong>Button buck</strong>: a male fawn with two small bumps, not antlers. Counts as antlerless (99%, synopsis page 3, via the <a href=\"#/s/white-tailed-deer\">quick lesson</a>).</li><li><strong>Yearling buck</strong> (about 1.5 years): often a spike or small fork, thin neck, \"a doe with antlers\" (65%, National Deer Association via Field and Stream).</li></ul></details><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Labelled white tailed buck. One main beam curving forward with single tines rising off it. Smaller ears than a mule deer. A wide tail, brown on top and white underneath, raised as a white flag when alarmed. A small leg gland. It runs with a smooth gallop, not a bounce.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White tail: what to look for</text><g transform=\"translate(230 200) scale(1.5 1.5)\"><rect x=\"-30\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"-21\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"22\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"31\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M26 -10 L42 -40 L56 -36 L40 6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"56\" cy=\"-40\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(18 56 -40)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"42\" cy=\"-50\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 42 -50)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"-42\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M48 -46 Q40 -70 62 -80 M44 -60 L40 -72 M46 -68 L46 -82 M54 -76 L56 -90\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-40 -8 Q-46 -26 -56 -32 Q-62 -26 -54 -14 Q-48 -4 -42 0 Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><line x1=\"296\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"296\" cy=\"96\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"236\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">One main beam,</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">tines rise off it</text><line x1=\"293\" y1=\"127\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"293\" cy=\"127\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"334\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Smaller</text><text x=\"334\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">ears</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"160\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Wide tail,</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">white under:</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"231\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">the flag</text><line x1=\"191\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"284\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"191\" cy=\"236\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"214\" y=\"289\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Small leg gland</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Rear views side by side. Left, white tailed deer: a wide brown tail with white only on the underside and edges, small white patch under it. Right, mule deer: a thin white rope tail with a black tip on a large white rump patch.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Look at the back end</text><rect x=\"71\" y=\"190\" width=\"12\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"127\" y=\"190\" width=\"12\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"52\" ry=\"50\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M91 150 Q 105 140 119 150 L 115 200 Q 105 206 95 200 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe4\"/><path d=\"M85 118 C 79 150 83 190 105 196 C 127 190 131 150 125 118 Q 105 108 85 118 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M85 118 L81 128 M125 118 L129 128\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><rect x=\"261\" y=\"190\" width=\"12\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"317\" y=\"190\" width=\"12\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"295\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"52\" ry=\"50\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"295\" cy=\"155\" rx=\"36\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><rect x=\"290\" y=\"120\" width=\"10\" height=\"56\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"290\" y=\"166\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">White tail</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mule deer</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wide brown tail,</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">white only underneath</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thin white tail, black tip,</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">big white rump patch</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"270\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>White tail: wide brown tail, white only underneath <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Up and waving = the <strong>flag</strong> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tail, rump and run</summary><ul><li>White tail: tail is wide, brown on top, bright white underneath and on the edges (85%, Alberta Institute for Wildlife Conservation).</li><li>Rump: only a small white patch, hidden when the tail is down <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Alarm: tail goes straight up and waves <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Mule deer: thin white rope tail with a black tip on a big white rump <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>The run: white tails gallop low and smooth to cover. Mule deer <strong>stot</strong>, bouncing on all 4 feet <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-buck-flag.jpg\" alt=\"White tailed buck running in snow with the tail up. The tail is the flag: broad, flipped up, white underneath.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>White tailed buck running in snow with the tail up. The tail is the flag: broad, flipped up, white underneath. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: ForestWander, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Whitetail-buck-running-snow_-_West_Virginia_-_ForestWander.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of one white tailed deer antler. A single main beam rises from the base and sweeps forward. A short brow tine, G1, sticks up near the base. Tines G2, G3 and G4 rise straight up off the top of the main beam. A note says hunters count tines about 2.5 cm or longer plus the beam tip.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">White tail antler: one beam, tines rise</text><path d=\"M300 262 C 300 215 282 172 232 146 C 192 126 142 128 98 146\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M297 222 l-14 -40\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M252 158 l-3 -62\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M204 134 l-3 -66\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M156 132 l-3 -52\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"305\" cy=\"270\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#c9b79c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Base (burr)</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Brow tine</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">(G1)</text><text x=\"264\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">G2</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">G3</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">G4</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Main beam</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">sweeps forward</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"196\" width=\"196\" height=\"88\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Count the points:</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">tines 2.5 cm (1 in) or</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">longer, plus beam tip</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">(hunter scoring, Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One main beam sweeps forward. Tines rise off it <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Mule deer antlers fork, and fork again <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to read white tail antlers</summary><ul><li><strong>Main beam</strong>: grows back from the base, then curves forward and in <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><strong>Brow tine</strong> (G1): short tine just above the base. Most white tail bucks have one <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Tines</strong> G2, G3, G4: rise straight up from the main beam, like teeth on a comb <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><strong>Counting points</strong>: hunters count each tine about 2.5 cm (1 in) or longer, plus the beam tip (Tip, scoring custom). For legal antler definitions use the <a href=\"#/s/rb-definitions\">Rule Book</a> only.</li><li>Antler size grows with age and food, but a young buck on good feed can fool you. Judge age by the body (next screen) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three white tailed bucks drawn side by side. A yearling has a thin neck, a slim body and long looking legs. A 2 to 3 year old has a fuller chest and a swelling neck. A buck 4 years or older has a deep chest, a sagging belly, a thick neck and legs that look short. Caption: judge body first, antlers second, from the side. Labelled as a tip.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Age a buck by body shape (Tip)</text><g><rect x=\"47\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"59\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"77\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"89\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M52 134 L30 102 L42 96 L58 128 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"26\" cy=\"98\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M32 92 c 0 -12 -6 -18 -16 -16 M28 86 l-1 -8 M22 80 l-2 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Yearling</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thin neck,</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">long legs</text></g><g><rect x=\"171\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"183\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"213\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"225\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"136\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M176 126 L154 94 L166 88 L188 120 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M156 84 c 0 -12 -6 -18 -16 -16 M152 78 l-1 -8 M146 72 l-2 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 to 3 years</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">chest fills,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">neck swells</text></g><g><rect x=\"297\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"36\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"309\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"36\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"347\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"36\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"359\" y=\"148\" width=\"6\" height=\"36\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"132\" rx=\"44\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"334\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M302 118 L280 86 L292 80 L324 112 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"276\" cy=\"82\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M282 76 c 0 -12 -6 -18 -16 -16 M278 70 l-1 -8 M272 64 l-2 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4 years plus</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">deep belly, thick</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">neck, legs look short</text></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Body first, antlers second. Judge from the side.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Body first, antlers second <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Yearling: thin neck, long legs, \"a doe with antlers\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: aging on the hoof</summary><ul><li><strong>Yearling</strong> (1.5 years): lanky, clear break between neck and shoulders, narrow waist <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>2 to 3 years</strong>: chest deepens, neck swells in the rut, hindquarters and shoulders even out <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><strong>4 years plus</strong>: deep chest, belly sags, thick neck blends into the shoulders, legs look short <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Old bucks may show loose skin on the face and neck and a sway back <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Hindquarters bigger than the shoulders: almost always a 1 or 2 year old <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Not an exact science. Get more than one view (65%, Kip Adams, National Deer Association, via Field and Stream).</li><li>Easiest in late pre rut and the weeks after, when bucks are in peak shape <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 420\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"420\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"410\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mule deer</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White tail</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Antlers (one side, seen from front)</text>\n  <!-- mule deer antler: forks that split again -->\n  <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M100 190 L100 160\"/>\n    <path d=\"M100 160 L70 110\"/>\n    <path d=\"M100 160 L130 110\"/>\n    <path d=\"M70 110 L55 72\"/>\n    <path d=\"M70 110 L85 75\"/>\n    <path d=\"M130 110 L118 74\"/>\n    <path d=\"M130 110 L148 76\"/>\n    <path d=\"M100 178 L86 168\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Forks that fork again</text>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(\"Y\" on a \"Y\")</text>\n  <!-- whitetail antler: one main beam, tines up -->\n  <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M250 190 Q240 120 300 100 Q345 90 360 120\"/>\n    <path d=\"M262 140 L258 112\"/>\n    <path d=\"M285 108 L282 72\"/>\n    <path d=\"M315 98 L318 64\"/>\n    <path d=\"M343 102 L350 76\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One main beam,</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">single tines up</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tail and rump (seen from behind)</text>\n  <!-- mule deer rump -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"330\" rx=\"48\" ry=\"48\" fill=\"#f3ead8\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"94\" y=\"290\" width=\"12\" height=\"62\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3ead8\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"94\" y=\"340\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"396\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Big white rump,</text>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"413\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thin tail, black tip</text>\n  <!-- whitetail flag -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"345\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"34\" fill=\"#b08a5e\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M300 340 C270 320 268 285 285 275 L300 270 L315 275 C332 285 330 320 300 340 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">flag up</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"396\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wide brown tail,</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"413\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">white below, waved up</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mule deer: separate species, separate licence and seasons <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Button buck = antlerless. Know which class is open <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Looks like</th><th>Tell</th><th>Legal note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mule deer</td><td>Rope tail, black tip, forks</td><td>Own seasons (<a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Rule Book</a>)</td></tr><tr><td>Doe</td><td>No bumps on head</td><td>Antlerless season only</td></tr><tr><td>Button buck</td><td>Two bumps</td><td>Antlerless <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Hybrid</td><td>Mixed traits</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> before you shoot</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: look alikes in detail</summary><ul><li><strong>Mule deer</strong>: big ears, rope tail with a black tip, forked antlers, stots <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. A separate species licence and separate seasons (99%, synopsis page 8 and region tables).</li><li><strong>Button buck</strong>: a male fawn. Its skin or hair covered bumps are not antlers, so it is antlerless (99%, synopsis page 3, <a href=\"#/s/rb-definitions\">Rule Book: definitions</a>).</li><li><strong>Hybrids</strong>: mule deer and white tails do cross. A genetic study on the western Canadian prairies found about 1% hybrids (85%, Russell and others 2021). Mixed tail and antler traits. If you cannot tell, do not shoot (Tip).</li><li><strong>Elk calf</strong>: much bigger, pale rump, dark neck <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Never confuse at legal range if you look (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<pre><code>\n&gt; [!warn]\n&gt; Study aid only. The official regulations are the law. Seasons and classes: [Rule Book: Region 3](#/s/rb-region-3), [Region 8](#/s/rb-region-8).\n\n</code></pre>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of white tailed deer live weights. Fawn at birth 2 to 4 kilograms. Average doe about 57 kilograms. Average buck about 91 kilograms. Mature buck 91 to 136 kilograms. Figures from Idaho and Montana agencies; BC weights not confirmed.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">How heavy? (live weight)</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fawn at birth</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">2 to 4 kg (5 to 8 lb)</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"62\" width=\"6\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"22\" y=\"62\" width=\"3\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Doe, average</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">about 57 kg (125 lb)</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"120\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Buck, average</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">about 91 kg (200 lb)</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"178\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mature buck</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">91 to 136 kg (200 to 300 lb)</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"236\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"253\" y=\"236\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Idaho and Montana figures. BC deer: VERIFY.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Average buck about 91 kg (200 lb), doe about 57 kg (125 lb) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>BC weights: not found. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: size detail</summary><ul><li>Idaho Fish and Game: bucks average 200 lb (91 kg), does 125 lb (57 kg) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Montana State University Extension: mature bucks 200 to 300 lb (91 to 136 kg); does 25 to 40% less, about 120 to 180 lb (54 to 82 kg) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Fawns weigh 5 to 8 lb (2 to 4 kg) at birth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span> and can double that in 2 weeks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Northern deer run bigger than southern deer (85%, US Forest Service species review: largest subspecies in the Northeast and Great Lakes, Florida Key deer the smallest).</li><li>White tails are smaller than mule deer on average in Idaho <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Does stop growing at 3 to 4 years, bucks at 4 to 5 (85%, US Forest Service species review).</li><li>Tip: a big white tail buck plus your pack is more than one trip. Plan the carry (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of white tailed deer killed by resident hunters in 2024, by BC region: Kootenay 3,971, Okanagan 2,225, Peace 1,542, Thompson 1,091, Cariboo 488, Omineca 308, Skeena 85, Lower Mainland none because there is no white tail season. The owner&#x27;s regions 3, 8 and 2 are orange.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">White tails taken by BC residents, 2024</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Region</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 Kootenay</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"52\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"356.0\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">3,971</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">8 Okanagan</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"82\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"268.0624527826744\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">2,225</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">7B Peace</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"112\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"233.6630571644422\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">1,542</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 Thompson</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"142\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"210.948375723999\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">1,091</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 Cariboo</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"172\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"180.57819189121128\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">488</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">7A Omineca</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"202\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"171.51246537396122\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">308</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">6 Skeena</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"232\" width=\"4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"160.28103752203475\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">85</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 Lower Mainland</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"262\" width=\"2\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"156.0\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">no season</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunter survey estimates. Orange: your 3 regions.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most BC white tails: Kootenay, Okanagan, Peace <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Region 2 Lower Mainland: no white tail season <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: populations and subspecies</summary><ul><li>Southern Interior white tails are the <strong>northwest white tail</strong>, Odocoileus virginianus ochrourus (75%, older BC publication via search preview).</li><li>Peace River white tails may be the prairie (Dakota) race (60%, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Historic core: the southeast (Kootenay) and northeast (Peace). They have spread into the south central Interior, including the Thompson (80%, BC provincial review, search preview).</li><li>Snow depth sets where they can live. They prefer valley bottoms with farmland (85%, BC account).</li><li>Resident hunter kills in 2024: Region 4 Kootenay 3,971; Region 8 Okanagan 2,225; Region 7B Peace 1,542; Region 3 Thompson 1,091; Region 5 Cariboo 488; Region 7A Omineca 308; Region 6 Skeena 85 (90%, BC Big Game Harvest Statistics, sample survey estimates).</li><li>Region 2: the page 14 table gives white tailed deer 0 for Region 2, and Herrling Island near Hope (MU, Management Unit, 2-3) has no open season (97%, synopsis pages 14 and 27).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of BC white tailed deer population estimates: about 40,000 in 1987, more than 113,000 in 2011, and a range of 35,000 to 71,500 in 2022. A note says the estimates use different methods, so compare with care.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">BC white tail numbers (estimates)</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"182\" width=\"70\" height=\"68\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\"1\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1987</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"174.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">40,000</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"58\" width=\"70\" height=\"192\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2011</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"49.900000000000006\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">113,000+</text><rect x=\"280\" y=\"128\" width=\"70\" height=\"122\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.45\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"190\" width=\"70\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"315\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2022</text><text x=\"315\" y=\"120.44999999999999\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">35,000 to 71,500</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Different methods: compare with care.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>About 40,000 (1987) to over 113,000 (2011) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>2022 estimate: 35,000 to 71,500 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Methods differ.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the numbers and why they disagree</summary><ul><li>BC provincial review: about 40,000 in 1987, rising to more than 113,000 by 2011 (80%, search preview).</li><li>Numbers dropped after the severe 1996 to 1997 winter, then recovered and spread <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Kootenay buck harvest and hunter success were lowest in 1997 and peaked in 2015 (75%, BC white tail questions and answers, 2017, search preview).</li><li>BC conservation status record: 2022 provincial estimate 35,000 to 71,500 (75%, search preview).</li><li>These two figures are far apart and no source explains why. Treat the true number as uncertain (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Near you: MU (Management Unit) 3-27 (Heffley Creek) residents killed 116, 97, 111, 145 and 133 white tails in 2020 to 2024, from about 600 to 790 hunters a year (90%, harvest statistics).</li><li>Hunter success in MU 3-27, 2024: about 17% (computed from 133 kills and 771 hunters) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grid of nine white tail numbers to remember: 310 degree field of view; a doe is in heat about 24 hours; if not bred she comes into heat again about 28 days later; the rut peaks in November; 4 stomach chambers; about 70 percent of yearling bucks leave home; fawns are hidden about 2 weeks; best hearing 4 to 8 kilohertz; licking branch 1.2 to 1.5 metres up.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">White tail numbers to remember</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"36\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">310°</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">field of view</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"36\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 h</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">doe in heat</text><rect x=\"268\" y=\"36\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">28 days</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">heat again</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"122\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nov</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rut peak</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"122\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stomachs</text><rect x=\"268\" y=\"122\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">70%</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">young bucks leave</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"208\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 wk</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fawn hidden</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"208\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4 to 8 kHz</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">best hearing</text><rect x=\"268\" y=\"208\" width=\"124\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1.2 to 1.5 m</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">licking branch</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Brown on top, white below; flag goes up, watch it go.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 1 beam, many tines. 2 deer in Region 3 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (tradition): \"Body first, antlers last.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks, mistakes and field drill</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Forks for mulies, combs for white; rope tail black, wide tail white.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 40, 113, 35 to 71: thousands of BC white tails, 1987, 2011, 2022.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (widely taught hunter wisdom, opinion): \"If you have to ask if it is legal, it is not.\" Echoes hunter education advice to be certain of your target.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"A flag is a goodbye, not a target.\" Matches the quick lesson's rule on running deer.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Calling a deer from one feature, like the tail, when it is half hidden.</li><li>Judging age by antlers alone.</li><li>Forgetting a button buck is antlerless and only legal in an antlerless season.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Next drive along the North Thompson: name every deer you see by tail, run and antlers. Say it out loud before you lift the binoculars.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Alberta Institute for Wildlife Conservation, <a href=\"https://www.aiwc.ca/blog/spotting-the-difference-a-guide-to-albertas-mule-deer-and-whitetails/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mule deer vs white tail ID</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Idaho Fish and Game, <a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/sites/default/files/wildlife-express_sept-2017-whitetalied-deer.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildlife Express: White tailed deer</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Knight, Montana State University Extension, <a href=\"https://animalrangeextension.montana.edu/wildlife/documents/whitetail-mgmt.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">White tailed deer management for Montana landowners</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>USDA Forest Service US Forest Service species review, <a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/animals/mammal/odvi/all.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">white tailed deer review</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Russell and others 2021, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8288014/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mule deer and white tail hybridization in western Canada</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Field and Stream, <a href=\"https://www.fieldandstream.com/hunting/how-to-age-whitetail-bucks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">how to age whitetail bucks</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>BC provincial white tail review, <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/fw/wildlife/management-issues/docs/white_tailed_deer_prov_review.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PDF</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Species and Ecosystems Explorer, <a href=\"https://a100.gov.bc.ca/pub/eswp/esr.do?id=16144\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">white tailed deer</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC <a href=\"https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/big-game-harvest-statistics-1976-to-2024\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Big Game Harvest Statistics 1976 to 2024</a>, checked 2026-10-04, figures computed 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, pages 3, 8, 14, 27, read directly 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Research log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-white-tailed-deer.md</code>.</li></ul>"]